    "body": "Hmm, I don't see how that's implicit. If I have\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconst obj1 = { o: 1 };\r\nconst obj2 = { o: 2 };\r\n\r\nconst arrayOfReferenceObjects = [obj1, obj2];\r\n\r\narrayOfReferenceObjects.forEach(obj => {\r\n  console.log(obj.o);\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\nI don't see anything in the above code (meant to approximate the spec) that \"implicitly\" allows the VM to rearrange `arrayOfReferenceObjects` into a different order, so that it prints 21 instead of 12. I think any VM that did so would not be compliant with the spec.",
